00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:33.150
- Classic predator-prey relationship.

00:24:33.150 --> 00:24:34.970
But neither one of these animals is bad

00:24:34.970 --> 00:24:36.770
just because of their role in nature.

00:24:36.770 --> 00:24:38.410
It's just the way nature works.

00:24:38.410 --> 00:24:40.730
- There are predator-prey relationships

00:24:40.730 --> 00:24:43.330
everywhere you look in the creature world.

00:24:43.330 --> 00:24:46.040
Like cheetahs and gazelles.

00:24:46.040 --> 00:24:48.580
Two of the fastest sprinters on the planet

00:24:48.580 --> 00:24:50.590
running for their lives.

00:24:50.590 --> 00:24:52.430
Coyotes and porcupines.

00:24:52.430 --> 00:24:54.230
With sharp quills like this,

00:24:54.230 --> 00:24:57.770
the porcupine goes up against the coyote's sharp teeth,

00:24:57.770 --> 00:24:59.670
quickness, and smarts.

00:25:01.150 --> 00:25:02.490
Spiders and insects.

00:25:03.860 --> 00:25:10.130
The spider uses its invisible web to capture moths, who would otherwise fly away from danger.

00:25:12.590 --> 00:25:14.800
Chameleons and grasshoppers.

00:25:15.400 --> 00:25:20.630
For these two, it's the quick-jumping reflexes of the grasshopper versus the chameleon's tongue.

00:25:21.560 --> 00:25:21.900
Whoa!

00:25:23.520 --> 00:25:25.440
And even toads and worms.

00:25:25.950 --> 00:25:30.000
You don't always think of toads as predators, but to a caterpillar, they are.

00:25:31.880 --> 00:25:35.320
So remember, every animal has to eat to survive.

00:25:35.320 --> 00:25:38.960
And in nature, some animals just fill the role of predator.

00:25:38.960 --> 00:25:40.370
It doesn't mean they're bad.

00:25:40.370 --> 00:25:41.900
And others are prey.

00:25:41.900 --> 00:25:45.430
Prey animals have great ways of defending themselves

00:25:45.430 --> 00:25:47.830
with amazing creature powers

00:25:47.830 --> 00:25:50.450
that make it really hard for predators.

00:25:50.450 --> 00:25:52.350
So hip hip for predators.

00:25:52.350 --> 00:25:53.830
And hooray for prey.

00:25:53.830 --> 00:25:56.030
Both are important in the creature world.

